    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks. so for the live load, i'm assuming i follow the standard 40 psf for residential? also, when looking at the beam spans, what are the main things that usually cause unexpected structural issues or sudden failure in cedar? like what should i be most worried about during the install?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "For residential decks, 40 psf (pounds per square foot) is a common standard for live load, but always verify this against the specific Vancouver building codes for your project type. When installing cedar, pay close attention to moisture exposure, as wood can warp, rot, or check if not properly treated or maintained. Hardware failure, such as rusted or inadequate fasteners, is also a major concern, so ensure all connectors are rated for exterior, wet environments.",
      "source": "target",
